{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nmanifest=json.loads(Path('task/resources/final/manifest.json').read_text())\nfor key,value in manifest.items():\n if key not in ['seeds','source']:\n  print(key,repr(value)[:650])\nprint('SOURCE',json.dumps(manifest.get('source'),indent=2))\nresource=json.loads(Path('task/resources/.agentic_resource_manifest.json').read_text())\nprint('RESOURCE manifest keys',list(resource))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"schema_version 1\nnormalization 'ordered finite little-endian float64 columns; signed zero normalized before SHA256; real=(Y,Yhat), synthetic=(X,Y). No text/feature extraction.'\nraw_shapes {'synthetic': [8320, 2], 'labeled': 128, 'unlabeled': 8192, 'smoke_labeled': 32, 'smoke_unlabeled': 256}\nsampling 'Synthetic independent Uniform(0,1) X, frozen f(X)=X, Bernoulli conditionals. NumPy PCG64 SeedSequence([seed,case_index,17923]). Real independent with-replacement labeled/unlabeled draws from unique normalized source groups; empirical-source mean, not external truth.'\nsplit 'Hash-sort normalized unique real records; first floor(unique/3) search, remainder final; duplicate groups never split. source_rows/group_offsets preserve original indices. Synthetic axes identify case, statistical seed, row; controls intentionally reuse nonlinear records.'\ndisjointness {'checked_before_features': True, 'cross_plane_normalized_hash_intersection': 0, 'search_hash_index_sha256': 'aca3f32b5923776138eb3f6f4152079ce3e672bf118463dd741149a7ded23d41', 'final_hash_index_sha256': '32e33339d0ad00851b9b569913399c15d849459efbba632c673b9a00eac86594'}\nfiles {'gene_expression.npz': 'd69ed1e0af709b6f42ec46a0c1f7e13cfb74cc4f05e10e84593bbf1e9a7101f4', 'linear.npz': 'f8f8ffa5ded064ccb44d0bbcc2f8699e4f95a1a5b5d64f205d625c50faf97ae3', 'nonlinear.npz': 'c86016a27d9025bfd4b90eaa7549a2a2e376a363800f3712c2d8059ae752efbf', 'rare_outcome.npz': 'd47c9954254a1e2f3a0eea6d9a9cb64cf985e5a205a66315bbeb029098ed42cf', 'raw_hashes.npy': '32e33339d0ad00851b9b569913399c15d849459efbba632c673b9a00eac86594', 'uninformative.npz': 'd1520de93f9a6adb20e6600b0a5189477fc98ff2372a6de58ecc329583eddfd3'}\ncontrols {'copy': 'identical infer endpoints within absolute 1e-12', 'reset': 'one first-case first-seed replay after all primary episodes; endpoints within 1e-10', 'constant_nonlinear': 'scores 0.5; require candidate label-only exact binomial interval within 1e-10', 'permuted_nonlinear': 'separate deterministic permutations of labeled/unlabeled nonlinear scores; reject identity or numeric-equivalent transformations; report paired width uncertainty, no compulsory no-gain threshold'}\naggregation 'Seven cases in stated order, equal seeds within case then 1/7 per case. Copy/reset diagnostics have zero score weight but are mandatory. Missing: coverage=0,ratio=100,utility=0,failure=1; hard integrity failure combined_score=-9.5. Score percase=mean utility-10*max(0,0.95-coverage).'\nscientific_limits 'Scientific_validity fixed conservative 0: arbitrary candidate theoretical variance assumptions cannot be certified by RPC. Empirical validity diagnostics with simultaneous uncertainty do not prove nominal coverage. correct means operational/integrity/evidence/control completion, not narrowing or publication readiness; honest negative findings eligible. Paper/theory/novelty/rights reviewed separately.'\nuncertainty 'Clopper-Pearson case coverage CIs with Bonferroni 7 cases and 4 methods (joint 95%); paired seed bootstrap 512 resamples, RNG seed 79231, percentile simultaneous differences at 0.05/(7*3), only for complete paired widths, otherwise null with fixed failure contributions retained.'\nSOURCE {\n  \"url\": \"https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&id=17PwlvAAKeBYGLXPz9L2LVnNJ66XjuyZd\",\n  \"download_sha256\": \"72565d2d88ed6a16331b3423da5dee036e97f2220fad054eb139ced1942e3303\",\n  \"repository_revision\": \"6b8475b53f0303e4abc4d1eb0b9