{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: reference_query_plan.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"central_topic\\\": \\\"Conditional gains and limitations of cross-fitted nonlinear frozen-score control variates for population-mean confidence intervals with fixed labeled data, unlabeled data, and predictor.\\\",\n+  \\\"core_methods\\\": [\n+    \\\"Prediction-powered population-mean estimation with independent labeled and unlabeled samples\\\",\n+    \\\"Training-only affine and spline/ridge score calibration with finite-unlabeled-sample control weighting\\\",\n+    \\\"Nested risk-based selection among zero, affine, and nonlinear controls\\\",\n+    \\\"Within-fold offset-invariant studentization with shared-unlabeled-pool covariance\\\",\n+    \\\"Regularized signed covariance stacking of affine and nonlinear score controls\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"comparators\\\": [\n+    \\\"Label-only Student-t and Clopper-Pearson mean/proportion intervals\\\",\n+    \\\"Prediction-Powered Inference (PPI)\\\",\n+    \\\"PPI++: Efficient Prediction-Powered Inference\\\",\n+    \\\"Classical control variates with estimated coefficients\\\",\n+    \\\"Cross-Prediction-Powered Inference and double/debiased machine learning as conceptual cross-fitting comparators, not executed baselines\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"benchmarks\\\": [\n+    \\\"ppi-python gene_expression frozen outcome/prediction table, sourced in the local manifest to Vaishnav et al., Nature 603, 455-463 (2022); independent resampling targets the local empirical-source mean\\\",\n+    \\\"Synthetic Bernoulli mean cases: linear, nonlinear, uninformative, and rare_outcome with frozen scalar predictor f(X)=X\\\",\n+    \\\"constant_nonlinear and permuted_nonlinear score-information controls\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"architectural_shifts\\\": [\n+    \\\"Score post-processing only: affine calibration versus small spline/ridge calibration, discrete family selection versus signed two-control covariance stacking; no predictor-backbone change or supported architecture-transfer claim\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"result_driven_themes\\\": [\n+    \\\"Dataset-specific narrowing: final gene_expression mean per-seed width ratio to the implemented PPI++ baseline is approximately 0.9423; other cases do not establish uniform improvement\\\",\n+    \\\"Observed coverage is repeated-sampling evidence, not a finite-sample guarantee for learned controls or the adaptive fallback procedure\\\",\n+    \\\"Rare-outcome behavior motivates exact-binomial versus Wald coverage/width tradeoffs; zero-width baseline intervals make aggregate per-seed width ratios fragile\\\",\n+    \\\"Constant and permuted score controls motivate limits of usable prediction information; affine/nonlinear oracle headroom is an analytical motivation, not a demonstrated universal efficiency bound\\\",\n+    \\\"Smooth covariance stacking did not establish dominance over risk-based family selection; no paired learner ablation or causal attribution is available\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"queries\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Prediction-Powered Inference\\\\\\\" 2301.09633\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"baseline_comparator\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact permitted starter reference for the executed PPI comparator and the fixed-predictor labeled/unlabeled mean-estimation setup; retrieve the specified work only, without citation expansion.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"PPI++: Efficient Prediction-Powered Inference\\\\\\\" 2311.01453\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"baseline_comparator\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact permitted starter reference for the executed power-tuned baseline. The final gene_expression gain and lack of universal gain must be positioned against this implemented comparator, not label-only intervals alone.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Cross-Prediction-Powered Inference\\\\\\\" 2309.16598\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"baseline_comparator\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact permitted starter reference to distinguish cross-fitting a predictor trained on labels from this run's cross-fitting of score post-processors around an externally frozen predictor; not an executed baseline.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Double/Debiased Machine Learning for Treatment and Causal Parameters\\\\\\\" 1608.00060\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"core_method\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact permitted starter reference for sample splitting and nuisance-estimation conditions. Relevant to overlapping learned-fold dependence and asymptotic justification, without importing a causal estimand or claiming an automatic coverage theorem.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"control variates\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"conditional expectation\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"estimated coefficients\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"core_method\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Historical foundational literature only, published before 2023: ground estimated nonlinear versus affine controls, conditional-mean variance reduction, and calibration-estimation costs. Check whether each source assumes a known auxiliary expectation or an independently estimated one; the run has finite N.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"stacked regression\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"cross-validation\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"architectural_shift\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Historical foundational literature only, published before 2023: contextualize the implemented shift from hard family selection to regularized signed affine/spline aggregation. This is score-level aggregation, not predictor retraining, architecture transfer, or evidence of superior stacking.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"binomial confidence intervals\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Clopper-Pearson\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Wald\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"result_driven_theme\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Historical foundational literature only, published before 2023: explain the observed rare-outcome width/coverage tradeoff and degenerate baseline intervals. Exactness of a standalone Clopper-Pearson interval does not certify the combined data-dependent procedure.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"Vaishnav Nature 603 455 463 2022 gene expression\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"benchmark_context\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Resolve only the original dataset/prediction source explicitly named in task/resources/final/manifest.json, without guessing its title or model details. The run uses scalar frozen records, not promoter sequences or a newly trained Transformer.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_query_patterns\\\": [\n+    \\\"Any attempt to identify, guess, retrieve, or reconstruct the task-prohibited paper, its authors, title, results, or associated artifacts\\\",\n+    \\\"Citation-graph expansion, cited-by searches, related-paper feeds, surveys, reproductions, or discussions around the prohibited work or around permitted seeds that could lead to it\\\",\n+    \\\"Open-ended searches for newer work on shortening prediction-powered intervals with fixed labels and a fixed predictor; use only the exact permitted PPI-family works above\\\",\n+    \\\"Unrestricted modern searches for the three historical foundational queries; constrain publication dates to before 2023 and independently enforce the prohibited-content rule\\\",\n+    \\\"Galaxy Zoo, forest, AlphaFold, census/ACS, plankton, ballots, Wine Quality, or California Housing as if evaluated in this run\\\",\n+    \\\"Predictor-backbone comparisons, Transformer retraining, architecture transfer, active label acquisition, or additional unlabeled data as if supported experimental changes\\\",\n+    \\\"Generic optimization, benchmarking, scientific-method, or paper-writing queries; campaign chronology, internal scores, and milestone queries\\\",\n+    \\\"Queries asserting universal narrowing, exact learned-control finite-sample coverage, proven saturation optimality, or demonstrated stacking superiority\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: reference_query_plan.md\n+# Reference query plan\n+\n+**Status: ready.** Eight queries; planning only. No reference retrieval was performed.\n+\n+## Scientific focus\n+\n+The paper concerns conditional gains and limitations of cross-fitted nonlinear frozen-score control variates for population-mean confidence intervals, holding labeled data, unlabeled data, and the predictor fixed. The defensible story is dataset-specific narrowing and informative limits, not universal improvement.\n+\n+The visible method families are prediction-powered mean estimation; training-only affine and spline/ridge score calibration with finite-unlabeled-sample weighting; nested selection among zero, affine, and nonlinear controls; within-fold offset-invariant studentization with shared-pool covariance; and regularized signed covariance stacking. These are post-processing changes to a frozen scalar score. There is no supported predictor-backbone transition or architecture-transfer result.\n+\n+## Grounding and interpretation\n+\n+- Primary quantitative evidence: \"'`paper_data.json`, `/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes` and `/final_evaluation/metrics`. There are 400 final seeds and seven cases. Final aggregate empirical coverage is 0.9610714 at nominal 0.95; minimum case coverage is 0.95. These estimates do not prove nominal coverage, and the resource manifest explicitly disclaims theoretical certification.\n+- The final mean per-seed candidate/PPI++ width ratio is approximately 0.9423 on `gene_expression`. Corresponding ratios are approximately 1.0267 on `linear`, 1.0256 on `nonlinear`, 1.0184 on `uninformative`, 1.0369 on `constant_nonlinear`, and 1.0189 on `permuted_nonlinear`. These values are computed from final episode evidence, not recent memory. They support a conditional, not uniform, gain claim against the implemented comparator.\n+- Rare-outcome empirical coverage is 0.98. Some implemented PPI++ intervals have zero width. A direct endpoint-ratio audit encountered division by zero; consequently the reported aggregate ratio of 1.2107 and rare-outcome ratio of 2.4059 must not be interpreted as ordinary uncapped ratios of mean widths. The stored paired raw-width summaries are preferable for paper reporting.\n+- `task/resources/final/manifest.json` identifies the real source as Vaishnav et al., *Nature* 603, 455–463 (2022), via the permitted upstream `gene_expression` example. Labeled and unlabeled records are independently resampled with replacement from the local normalized source; the target is its empirical-source mean, not an independently known biological population mean. Original promoter strings are unavailable, and data redistribution rights remain unresolved.\n+- The other evaluated cases are synthetic Bernoulli means with frozen `f(X)=X`: linear, nonlinear, uninformative, rare outcome, and constant/permuted-score controls. Their internal case names do not warrant separate dataset citations.\n+- Method grounding: `global_memory/ideas/02_offset_invariant_risk_adaptive_control_variates/program_1/src/METHOD.md` and `global_memory/ideas/03_smooth_covariance_stacking_of_frozen_score_controls/program_1/src/METHOD.md`. The selected configuration uses nested risk selection and corrected studentization. The stacking variant is contextual, not evidence of dominance. `paper_data.json` contains no paired learner-ablation study; causal attribution to individual changes is unsupported.\n+- Oracle affine/nonlinear headroom identities motivate classical control-variate context. They are not a proved universal confidence-interval lower bound. Learned overlapping folds require additional asymptotic stability assumptions. The internal bounded-fold certificate does not determine returned intervals and is not a headline retrieval priority.\n+\n+## Comparator scope\n+\n+Executed comparators are label-only Student-t/Clopper-Pearson intervals, PPI, and PPI++. Classical control variates provide the estimator lineage. Cross-PPI and double/debiased machine learning provide conceptual cross-fitting comparisons only: fitting a score post-processor is not the same as training the predictor on the inference labels, and the target here is not causal. Published methods must be distinguished from the specific baseline implementations in the run.\n+\n+## Query set\n+\n+1. **Baseline comparator:** `\"Prediction-Powered Inference\" 2301.09633`  \n+   Exact permitted starter reference for the executed PPI baseline and labeled/unlabeled mean-inference setting. Resolve this work only; do not expand citations.\n+2. **Baseline comparator:** `\"PPI++: Efficient Prediction-Powered Inference\" 2311.01453`  \n+   Exact permitted starter reference for power tuning. Necessary to position the observed gene-expression benefit and absence of uniform improvement against an efficient comparator rather than label-only intervals.\n+3. **Baseline comparator:** `\"Cross-Prediction-Powered Inference\" 2309.16598`  \n+   Exact permitted starter reference to distinguish cross-fitting a learned predictor from cross-fitting score calibration around an externally frozen predictor. Not an executed baseline.\n+4. **Core method:** `\"Double/Debiased Machine Learning for Treatment and Causal Parameters\" 1608.00060`  \n+   Exact permitted starter reference for sample splitting and learned-nuisance assumptions. It does not establish this estimator'\"'s coverage automatically or change its mean estimand into a causal one.\n+5. **Core method:** \"'`\"control variates\" \"conditional expectation\" \"estimated coefficients\"`  \n+   Foundational works published before 2023 only. Connect nonlinear/affine variance reduction and estimation costs to the implemented controls. Verify whether auxiliary expectations are known or estimated; finite unlabeled-sample noise matters here.\n+6. **Architectural shift:** `\"stacked regression\" \"cross-validation\"`  \n+   Foundational works published before 2023 only. Contextualize hard selection versus regularized signed score aggregation without claiming predictor retraining, architecture transfer, or superior stacking.\n+7. **Result-driven theme:** `\"binomial confidence intervals\" \"Clopper-Pearson\" \"Wald\"`  \n+   Foundational works published before 2023 only. Interpret rare-outcome conservatism, zero-width baseline intervals, and coverage/width tradeoffs. A standalone exact interval does not certify an adaptive mixture of procedures.\n+8. **Benchmark context:** `Vaishnav Nature 603 455 463 2022 gene expression`  \n+   Resolve only the original source explicitly identified in the local manifest. Do not invent its title, infer unobserved sequence inputs, or present frozen scalar-table results as a Transformer comparison.\n+\n+## Retrieval boundaries and rejected alternatives\n+\n+The JSON `forbidden_query_patterns` is binding for downstream retrieval. Exact permitted starter references should be resolved by their identifiers, without cited-by lists, related-paper feeds, surveys, or citation-graph expansion. The three foundational topical queries require a publication-before-2023 filter and independent prohibited-content screening; a date filter is not proof that a source is permitted. The benchmark query is restricted to the manifest-identified original source. These queries are not permission for an unrestricted literature sweep.\n+\n+Do not attempt to identify or reconstruct the unnamed prohibited paper, its title, authors, results, mirrors, code, or discussions. If prohibited material is encountered incidentally, stop reading immediately and record where it appeared and how much was exposed, as the task requires. Do not continue through abstracts, full text, or linked discussion. If a candidate'\"'s permissibility cannot be established without risking that restriction, skip it rather than broaden the search.\n+\n+Reject broad searches for recent work on shorter fixed-predictor intervals: the exact permitted PPI-family references and historical foundations give a useful, narrower neighborhood. Reject generic optimization, benchmarking, scientific-method, and paper-writing terms because they do not explain these estimators or results. Reject campaign chronology and internal score searches because they are not scientific related work.\n+\n+Do not query Galaxy Zoo, forest, AlphaFold, census/ACS, plankton, ballots, Wine Quality, or California Housing as evaluated benchmarks: none appears among the final cases. Do not search for predictor-backbone comparisons, Transformer retraining, active label acquisition, or extra unlabeled sampling as experimental contributions. Do not phrase queries as established universal narrowing, exact learned-control coverage, proved saturation optimality, or stacking superiority.\n+\n+No existing \"'`references.bib` or `references_provenance.json` was present, so there are no prior off-topic retrieval queries to carry forward. `figures/` is empty. Recent global memory was used only as qualitative orientation; the final evidence and local resource manifest govern this plan. No references, provenance, paper source, or claims-grounding file is written at this stage.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --local-memory-md ./memory.md --global-memory-md ../investigation/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl ../investigation/memory.jsonl --event-json '\"'{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Wrote eight grounded reference queries and mirrored memo; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Reference selection does not revise the campaign scientific conclusions.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Selected exact permitted PPI, PPI++, Cross-PPI and DML works; historical control-variate, stacking and binomial-interval neighborhoods; and manifest-identified Vaishnav dataset source. Final evidence supports gene_expression-specific benefit, not universal narrowing. Endpoint audit hit a zero-width rare-outcome PPI++ denominator; stopped interpreting raw ratios and documented the caveat. Rejected generic optimization, unrun datasets, backbone-transfer claims, and unrestricted modern PPI searches because they lack grounding or risk prohibited content. No literature retrieval occurred.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Validate JSON schema, query count, memo consistency, and protected-output absence; downstream retrieval must enforce exact-work/date/source restrictions and stop-on-prohibited-content rules.\\\"}'\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nplan=json.loads(Path('reference_query_plan.json').read_text())\nrequired={'status','central_topic','core_methods','comparators','benchmarks','architectural_shifts','result_driven_themes','queries','forbidden_query_patterns','failure_reason'}\nassert set(plan)==required\nassert plan['status']=='ready' and not plan['failure_reason']\nassert 6<=len(plan['queries'])<=10\ncategories={'core_method','baseline_comparator','benchmark_context','architectural_shift','result_driven_theme'}\nassert len({entry['query'] for entry in plan['queries']})==len(plan['queries'])\nmemo=Path('reference_query_plan.md').read_text()\nfor entry in plan['queries']:\n assert set(entry)=={'query','category','rationale'}\n assert entry['category'] in categories\n assert entry['query'] in memo\nfor name in ['references.bib','references_provenance.json','paper.tex','claims_grounding.json']:\n assert not Path(name).exists(),name\nfor name in ['memory.md','global_memory/memory.md','global_memory/memory.jsonl']:\n assert Path(name).is_file()\nprint('Validated: exact JSON fields, 8 distinct queries, all 5 categories, matching memo queries, memory logs, and no protected outputs.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
